<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dumnorix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 54 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dumnorix was a nobleman of the Aedui in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diviciacus-suessiones">Diviciacus</a>. He led the anti-Roman party among his people, married a Helvetian noblewoman and helped the Helvetii in their migration of 58 BCE. In 54 BCE he refused to join Caesar's expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and was killed by Caesar's cavalry while trying to escape.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dumnorix.jpg" alt="Dumnorix" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Urban · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bibracte_aristocrate_gaulois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
